  "content": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "Limits, sequences, series, and polynomial behaviour give students the conceptual scaffolding for calculus — and appear on the hardest ACT questions.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Limit intuition",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\lim_{x\\to a}f(x) \\) — value \\( f \\) approaches",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Geometric series",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\dfrac{a_1}{1-r},\\ |r|<1 \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Binomial theorem",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( (a+b)^n=\\sum\\binom{n}{k}a^{n-k}b^k \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Parametric",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( x=f(t),\\ y=g(t) \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 5.A",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "Evaluate \\( \\displaystyle\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty}3\\left(\\tfrac{1}{2}\\right)^{n-1} \\). \\[ S=\\frac{3}{1-\\tfrac{1}{2}}=\\frac{3}{\\tfrac{1}{2}}=6. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "def",
        "label": {
          "en": "● Limits & Conic Sections",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<strong>Informal limit:</strong> \\(\\lim_{x \\to a}f(x) = L\\) means \\(f(x)\\) approaches \\(L\\) as \\(x\\) approaches \\(a\\). <strong>Conic sections</strong> — standard forms: circle \\((x-h)^2+(y-k)^2=r^2\\); ellipse \\(\\dfrac{x^2}{a^2}+\\dfrac{y^2}{b^2}=1\\); hyperbola \\(\\dfrac{x^2}{a^2}-\\dfrac{y^2}{b^2}=1\\); parabola \\(y=ax^2+bx+c\\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example — Identify and graph a conic",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "Identify the conic: \\(4x^2 + 9y^2 = 36\\). <p>Divide by 36: \\(\\dfrac{x^2}{9}+\\dfrac{y^2}{4}=1\\). This is an <strong>ellipse</strong> with \\(a=3\\) along \\(x\\)-axis and \\(b=2\\) along \\(y\\)-axis, centre \\((0,0)\\).</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "practiceProblem",
        "question": {
          "en": "Find \\(\\lim_{x \\to 3}\\dfrac{x^2-9}{x-3}\\).",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "Factor: \\(\\dfrac{(x-3)(x+3)}{x-3} = x+3\\). As \\(x \\to 3\\): limit \\(= 6\\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      }
    ]
  },
